D=[
{'title':'Objective 1 · Design and integrate the hardware','status':'Achieved at prototype integration level','goal':'Interface the sensing, display, alert and timekeeping hardware with the ESP32 to acquire vital-sign signals and support local monitoring.','steps':['Connected MAX30102 and MLX90614 on shared I²C: GPIO4 SDA and GPIO5 SCL. Their addresses, 0x57 and 0x5A, responded with zero bus errors.','Connected DS1302 on GPIO6/7/14, ST7789 on GPIO8–12 and microSD on GPIO21/40/41/42. The implemented display/RTC replaced the proposed LCD/DS3231.','Added local outputs: buzzer on GPIO15 and RGB on GPIO16/17/18. Display text/colour bars and command-driven buzzer beeps were observed.','Produced the schematic and two-layer SPI carrier. Recorded ERC, DRC, unrouted and schematic-parity issues were all zero.'], 'numbers':[['2 sensors','I²C devices responded at 0x57 and 0x5A'],['91,561–105,770','MAX30102 infrared counts with finger; about 700 uncovered'],['25.97–30.73 °C','Observed MLX90614 surface readings, not neonatal body temperatures'],['4 / 4','SD diagnostic attempts passed']], 'meaning':'The numbers demonstrate that the hardware exchanged signals, acquired changing sensor data, displayed output and stored records. They do not establish calibrated measurement accuracy.','limits':'Finger-test heart-rate estimates ranged from 42 to 187 bpm without a reference instrument. The maximum surface-to-ambient difference was 0.84 °C, below the configured 1.5 °C warm-target condition, so no warm-target events were recorded. Battery endurance and clinical accuracy remain unverified.','source':'Reviewed report §§7.3.2–7.3.6'},
{'title':'Objective 2 · Develop the connected software','status':'Achieved as a working prototype','goal':'Build firmware, a Flask/PostgreSQL backend and a React dashboard with local threshold alerts, offline buffering, synchronisation and explainable AI.','steps':['Firmware samples and validates readings, timestamps them and applies bedside threshold rules. Invalid or removed-sensor readings are marked unavailable rather than interpreted as normal.','The local display, LED and buzzer do not wait for a network connection or AI response. microSD preserves queued records during connectivity loss.','On reconnection, firmware sends JSON records to the Flask API. The backend authenticates the request and persists readings, sessions and alerts in PostgreSQL.','The backend calculates advisory risk/trend information; React presents current and historical readings, alerts and explanations for a nurse to review.'], 'numbers':[['588 / 230','Rows saved in two analysed diagnostic runs'],['0 / 0','Sampler resets / temperature-packet errors in both runs'],['HTTP 200','Runtime, heartbeat and sync requests in both runs'],['120 s → 12','Causal history window → AI features: last, mean, slope and variation for three vital signs']], 'meaning':'The recorded runs support working storage and device-to-backend communication. HTTP 200 indicates successful request handling; it does not prove clinical correctness or a guaranteed delivery time.','limits':'Saved-row counts are from different diagnostic runs, not an end-to-end loss-rate experiment. Controlled offline recovery, dashboard delay and production reliability were not fully quantified. AI is advisory and does not gate local alerts.','source':'Reviewed report §§7.4.1–7.4.6'},
{'title':'Objective 3 · Test components and integrated dataflow','status':'Partly achieved','goal':'Test hardware, firmware, backend and dashboard individually and together, including connectivity, API behaviour and access control.','steps':['Compiled and uploaded firmware; verified the programmed flash hash. Scanned the sensor bus and exercised the display, buzzer, RGB and microSD.','Tested SD write, read, append, compare and delete operations; repeated SD verification while RGB output states were active.','Ran firmware tests for threshold alarms, temperature-packet validation, stale readings, finger removal and heart-rate averaging safeguards.','Ran backend checks for authentication, access control, reading round-trip, quality-aware alerts, pagination, clock validation and synchronisation retry/rate-limit handling.'], 'numbers':[['21 / 21','Backend tests passed at the recorded checkpoint'],['4','Database migrations applied to a fresh database'],['0','Reported schema differences after migration'],['345,966 B / 24,912 B','Flash / static RAM for the display-and-sensor diagnostic build']], 'meaning':'These results support functional integration, persistence and the tested access-control paths. Passing tests is not a clinical validation study or a complete security audit.','limits':'No verified reference-instrument accuracy dataset, controlled sampling jitter/alert-latency study, complete 5/15/30-minute offline trials, 20-cycle Wi-Fi recovery study or measured dashboard delay was available. This is why the testing objective is only partly achieved.','source':'Reviewed report §§7.3.4, 7.5.1–7.5.5'},
{'title':'Objective 4 · Evaluate performance against a baseline','status':'Partly achieved','goal':'Evaluate real-time performance, accuracy, alert timing and AI false-warning burden/lead time against threshold-only detection.','steps':['Generated 480 controlled synthetic sessions across eight scenarios. Split by session: 288 training, 96 validation and 96 test, keeping test sessions held out.','Selected the logistic-regression decision threshold of 0.75 using validation data. Evaluated on 19,272 held-out synthetic rows.','Counted row-level outcomes: 4,395 true positives, 13,605 true negatives, 292 false positives and 980 false negatives.','Compared simulated event detection and warning burden with the threshold-only baseline, rather than claiming that a higher AI score proves clinical benefit.'], 'numbers':[['93.77%','Precision = 4,395 / (4,395 + 292)'],['81.77%','Recall = 4,395 / (4,395 + 980)'],['44 / 49 vs 25 / 49','Events detected at onset: AI versus threshold-only'],['107.5 s vs 0 s','Median simulated detection lead time']], 'meaning':'AI detected 19 more simulated events at onset. Event sensitivity increased from 51.0% to 89.8% (38.8 percentage points). ROC-AUC was 0.9748, a ranking measure—not “97.48% accuracy”.','limits':'False-warning episodes increased from 0.7472 to 1.4197 per simulated hour. Earlier detection therefore came with more warnings. Row-level false positives and warning episodes are different measures. Synthetic labels are not verified neonatal outcomes; reference accuracy, timing and clinical performance remain unestablished.','source':'Reviewed report §§7.6.1–7.6.5'}]
